" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These letter dynamic symbols are separated from crescendo, decrescendo, and wedge indications. Dynamic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation is inconsistent in scores. Many things are assumed by the composer and left out, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns to original dynamics. The MusicXML format captures what is in the score, but does not try to be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal for analysis or synthesis of dynamics."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute is used when the dynamics are associated with a note. It is ignored when the dynamics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are associated with a direction. In that case the direction element’s placement attribute is used instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<dynamics>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "